.Dd September 24, 2026
.Dt DOOM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm doom
.Nd play Doom on the framebuffer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl mb Ar N
.Op Fl iwad Ar path
.Op Ar engine-options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the doomgeneric engine with a Rach2 platform layer.
The static executable
.Pa /bin/doom
uses its own small runtime over nine system calls and does not link musl.
.Pp
Graphics use VGA mode 13h through the framebuffer device.
Frames are 320 by 200 palette indices.
The 256-entry palette is set through
.Dv FB_SETPALETTE .
.Pp
Keyboard input consists of PS/2 set 1 scan codes read from standard input.
The port maps letters, digits, arrows, modifiers, function keys, Enter,
Escape, Tab, and the Doom action keys.
The input queue holds at most 31 unread key transitions.
Mouse input uses three-byte packets when the mouse device opens;
otherwise only keyboard input is used.
.Pp
Time is read with
.Xr gettimeofday 2 .
Sleep is a busy wait.
The port provides PCM sound, PC speaker sound, and music synthesized
with Nuked OPL3.
.Pp
A WAD game-data file is required.
Without one the engine prints
.Ql IWAD file '/demo/doom1.wad' not found\&!
on standard error, the devices are closed, and
.Nm
exits with status 255.
The build stages the shareware WAD at
.Pa /demo/doom1.wad
as an optional file when it is present at build time.
The default WAD, framebuffer and mouse paths are absolute, so the game
can start from any directory.
Arguments are forwarded to the engine.
.Fl iwad Ar path
overrides the default WAD; a relative path uses the current directory.
.Pp
The zone allocation starts at 16 MiB.
The platform suggests whole MiB of free memory minus 8 MiB;
only suggestions from 6 through 15 MiB replace the initial request.
Smaller suggestions leave it at 16 MiB.
Failed allocations are retried in 1 MiB steps down to 6 MiB.
.Fl mb Ar N
requests exactly N MiB without those retries.
Pages are allocated on first access, so allocation success does not
guarantee enough physical memory.
.Pp
Confirming Quit in the menu runs the engine's exit callbacks, closes the
devices, restores text mode, prints the final performance report and
exits with status zero.
The report also appears every ten seconds and includes the allocated zone size.
.Pp
Normal save slots do not work.
The runtime's directory creation, removal and rename stubs always fail.
The engine can report a successful save without updating the slot.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /demo/doom1.wad
.It Pa /bin/doom
Static game executable.
.It Pa /fb
Framebuffer device.
.It Pa /mouse
Optional mouse device.
.It Pa /demo/doom1.wad
Game data, supplied separately.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl doom -mb 10
.Pp
In the source tree,
.Ql tests/run doom
first starts the game with the WAD moved away and requires that error
and status 255, then launches the game from
.Pa /root ,
checks that it remains running after ten seconds, checks framebuffer
initialization and a zone of at least 10 MiB, and counts disk commands.
It does not judge visual or audible quality.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gettimeofday 2 ,
.Xr console 4 ,
.Xr rach2 7
